      "llm_answer_preview": "The outline beats don\u2019t give a specific destination or location name for where Bonogo ends up. What they do establish is that once the rope is torn free, he\u2019s carried downstream by the river. One beat explicitly says \u201cBonogo flows downstream and has a wonderful zen underwater adventure,\u201d which frames it more as an experience than a mapped endpoint.\n\nIn response, Stafl and Caelynn cut loose a dinghy and let the river take them after him, using a lit net and hope to track or catch him, so the action continues along the same downstream path. The broader setting for this sequence is the Stone Bridge town flood-and-rescue set-piece, indicating the river run happens through or past that area.\n\nAfterward, the beats confirm he is eventually rescued, but they don\u2019t specify where along the river that occurs. So the only supported answer is: he\u2019s swept downstream, having an extended underwater drift, with no precise landing point given in the outline.",
